WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.204
"The headline result is that NeuPL is both more
efficient and more robust than comparable PSRO baselines.

00:00:04.284 --> 00:00:08.488
With a maximum population of eight policies,

00:00:08.568 --> 00:00:12.772
a NeuPL population successfully exploits PSRO
populations of the same eight policies

00:00:12.852 --> 00:00:17.056
even when each PSRO iteration was given twice as
many gradient steps.

00:00:17.136 --> 00:00:21.340
Crucially,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.624
the gain in relative population performance
coincides with growth in the effective population size,

00:00:25.704 --> 00:00:29.908
from five up to eight distinct policies,

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:34.192
showing that the improvement comes from genuinely
discovering new strategies rather than overfitting.

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:38.476
Both continued-training and from-scratch PSRO
variants prove equally exploitable,

00:00:38.556 --> 00:00:42.760
suggesting they fail to build reusable representations."
